1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,105
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,105 --> 00:00:09,005
This morning the system named no pick, so tonight there is nothing to grade.

3
00:00:09,005 --> 00:00:13,740
No setup, no trade, no loss — that is the discipline working.

4
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:18,676
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

5
00:00:18,676 --> 00:00:24,085
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

6
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:28,510
On the day, the book is down 275 dollars.

7
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:35,146
Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (TSM) leads, +1.0 percent.

8
00:00:35,146 --> 00:00:41,346
First Trust NASDAQ Cybersecurity ETF (CIBR) lags at -1.8.

9
00:00:41,346 --> 00:00:47,221
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

10
00:00:47,221 --> 00:00:50,747
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

11
00:00:50,703 --> 00:00:58,221
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

12
00:00:58,221 --> 00:01:08,378
12 positions, led by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing, ticker TSM, APA Corporation, ticker APA, Arista Networks, ticker ANET.

13
00:01:08,378 --> 00:01:19,255
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

14
00:01:19,217 --> 00:01:24,550
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

15
00:01:24,550 --> 00:01:27,216
Every morning OROS proposes.

16
00:01:27,216 --> 00:01:38,929
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

17
00:01:38,929 --> 00:01:43,405
Inside the book today: 2 positions up, 10 down.

18
00:01:43,405 --> 00:01:46,071
Best, NVDA at +1.34 percent.

19
00:01:46,071 --> 00:01:48,071
Worst, SMCI at -3.12.

20
00:01:48,071 --> 00:01:53,594
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

21
00:01:53,594 --> 00:02:01,498
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -4.95% per trade over 340 graded positions.

22
00:02:01,498 --> 00:02:09,307
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 25% position size.

23
00:02:09,307 --> 00:02:15,021
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

24
00:02:15,021 --> 00:02:32,543
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 216 names close the day in Stage 2; 2 new invalidations queue exit reviews; position size stays cut to 25% until the record earns it back.

25
00:02:32,499 --> 00:02:34,714
Over to the sports desk.

26
00:02:34,714 --> 00:02:43,850
Day 55 of the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

27
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:48,649
In first place, the index fund, in gray, at 101,386.

28
00:02:48,649 --> 00:02:55,386
Then the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, 1.9 thousand back at 99,489.

29
00:02:55,386 --> 00:03:02,493
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 4.0 thousand back at 97,408.

30
00:03:02,493 --> 00:03:05,077
The race has no finish line.

31
00:03:05,077 --> 00:03:09,322
Same books, same dollars, back at it tomorrow.

32
00:03:09,322 --> 00:03:14,121
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

33
00:03:14,121 --> 00:03:15,967
Nothing is restated.

34
00:03:15,967 --> 00:03:24,874
On screen, three equity lines grown from the same starting dollar: the frozen first book, the live book, and the index fund.

35
00:03:24,836 --> 00:03:32,171
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

36
00:03:32,171 --> 00:03:34,412
Nothing here is financial advice.

37
00:03:34,412 --> 00:03:37,401
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
